cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ReliabilityLab in academic work, please cite this software."
title: "ReliabilityLab"
type: software
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-08-17"
authors:
  - family-names: "Amankwatia"
    given-names: "Manuel Bobie"
repository-code: "https://github.com/MBobie/ReliabilityLab"
license: "MIT"
abstract: >-
  ReliabilityLab is an open-source framework for evaluating machine-learning
  and NLP systems beyond clean benchmark accuracy. It currently supports
  training-data sensitivity analysis, stochastic text perturbations,
  probabilistic corruption severity, repeated robustness evaluation,
  confidence intervals, paired cross-model comparisons, and reproducible
  experiment artifacts.
keywords:
  - machine learning
  - natural language processing
  - robustness
  - reliability
  - reproducibility
  - intent classification
  - model evaluation
